  "rationale": "The official posted notice (retained-agenda) states 'THE REDISTRICTING COMMISSION WILL MEET IN OPEN SESSION ON SATURDAY, JANUARY 22, 2022' at Pleasant Oaks Recreation Center in Dallas, with a 'Redistricting Town Hall' agenda (Welcome/Chairman Jesse Oliver, Redistricting Overview, Census Update, public comments) and a City Secretary of Dallas posting stamp, so the convened body is the Dallas Redistricting Commission; 'Saturday' in the recording title is the meeting day, not a distinct body. The provider-player page confirms the video sits on the Dallas Swagit channel titled 'Saturday Redistricting Commission on January 22, 2022.' This matches the existing feed dallas-tx-redistricting-commission ('Meetings of the Dallas Redistricting Commission'). The town-hall format is the Commission's own open-session meeting with routine public comment, so per policy no Public Info feed membership is added, and no other body (e.g., City Council or bond bodies) is proven to have convened or jointly participated. Venue and topic words were not used to establish identity beyond the notice's explicit body name."
